From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tfrecomp <tfrecomp@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:12:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] native: the host program hears the log and the reason
 for an abort

A program that loads DXMT's libraries itself has no Wine console and may
not be reading DXMT's log file.  New header
include/native/dxmt_native_host.h: the host registers a log function and
an abort function, once, in winemetal.dylib (new file
src/nativemetal/host_hooks.c), which dxgi and d3d11 both link against.

The logger (one copy, in dxgi.dylib; d3d11 calls that copy) hands every
line to the log function before it writes it; a non-zero answer means
"do not write it".  Error lines reach the function even when
DXMT_LOG_LEVEL would drop them.

DXMTHostAbort(message) calls the abort function and then abort().  It
replaces the bare abort() of UNIMPLEMENTED (19 sites), of _massert
(D3D11_ASSERT), of the pure-virtual handler, of the swap chain
constructor and of the internal command library.  winemetal.dylib also
defines __assert_rtn, which Apple's assert() calls, so that in a build
with assertions a failed assert() of any of the three libraries goes the
same way instead of straight into libSystem's abort().

Two debug-level lines in the shader compile task ("Shader variant from
cache", "Shader variant converted") let a host count how much of a run
was served by the shader cache.

Wine builds are unchanged: util_host.hpp gives them an abort() and a log
function that does nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
